1
00:00:04,789 --> 00:00:09,900
Whiskers and Luna's World. Episode four. Mountains and Volcanoes!

2
00:00:17,283 --> 00:00:21,189
Luna, why is your globe so bumpy? Did it get goosebumps?

3
00:00:21,389 --> 00:00:23,337
Those bumps are mountains, Whiskers!

4
00:00:23,537 --> 00:00:25,236
But how does a mountain grow?

5
00:00:25,436 --> 00:00:28,380
I'll show you. Pip, push the other end of the blanket!

6
00:00:33,369 --> 00:00:38,063
The ground is made of giant pieces. They push together, very, very slowly.

7
00:00:38,263 --> 00:00:42,316
And where they push, the land folds up, like this. That's how mountains grow!

8
00:00:48,502 --> 00:00:52,030
Hey, my blanket is a mountain now. Nap Mountain!

9
00:00:54,624 --> 00:00:56,972
Which mountain is the tallest in the world?

10
00:00:57,172 --> 00:00:59,611
Let's go and see! Hold on to the cushion!

11
00:01:09,987 --> 00:01:12,270
Up, up into space they flew!

12
00:01:19,653 --> 00:01:21,637
There are mountains all over the world.

13
00:01:21,837 --> 00:01:24,892
But the tallest ones are here, in Asia. The Himalayas!

14
00:01:25,092 --> 00:01:26,772
The Him-a-what? Bless you.

15
00:01:42,535 --> 00:01:45,765
They landed high up in the Himalaya mountains.

16
00:01:48,958 --> 00:01:52,750
Welcome to the roof of the world. I'm Tashi, a snow leopard.

17
00:01:52,950 --> 00:01:56,566
And that is Mount Everest. The tallest mountain on Earth!

18
00:02:01,555 --> 00:02:06,601
It's almost nine kilometres high. Taller than twenty big skyscrapers, stacked up!

19
00:02:14,583 --> 00:02:17,503
But Bluebell said the deepest ocean is even deeper!

20
00:02:17,703 --> 00:02:20,546
She's right. Everest could hide in it, top and all!

21
00:02:26,133 --> 00:02:28,720
Brrr! Why is it so cold up here?

22
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:33,378
The higher you go, the colder it gets. So there's snow on top, even in summer.

23
00:02:40,762 --> 00:02:44,237
Snow in summer? I want a warm mountain, please.

24
00:02:44,437 --> 00:02:47,235
I know a mountain that's hot inside. A volcano!

25
00:02:47,435 --> 00:02:49,697
Goodbye, little ones. Fly safely!

26
00:02:57,080 --> 00:03:01,755
Away they flew, to the Galapagos Islands, in the Pacific Ocean.

27
00:03:12,131 --> 00:03:14,451
Ooh! A giant pot of hot chocolate!

28
00:03:14,651 --> 00:03:18,473
Ha! That's a volcano, my furry friend. I'm Iggy, an iguana.

29
00:03:18,673 --> 00:03:21,741
Deep inside is magma. Rock so hot, it melts!

30
00:03:26,730 --> 00:03:28,782
And when it comes out, we call it lava.

31
00:03:32,573 --> 00:03:34,114
The ground is shaking!

32
00:03:34,314 --> 00:03:37,238
Stay up there, nice and far away. She's erupting!

33
00:03:45,818 --> 00:03:50,135
Lava? Perfect for toasting my fish. From far, far away.

34
00:03:58,117 --> 00:04:00,110
Hot! Hot! Hot! It's charcoal!

35
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:03,281
Lava is hotter than any oven. Never go near it!

36
00:04:03,481 --> 00:04:06,270
I knew that. I made it crispy on purpose.

37
00:04:09,164 --> 00:04:12,853
Look. When lava cools down, it turns into hard new rock.

38
00:04:17,243 --> 00:04:21,497
My whole island was made by a volcano. Lots of islands were!

39
00:04:34,268 --> 00:04:38,541
Remember! One. Mountains grow when the land pushes together.

40
00:04:41,435 --> 00:04:45,270
Two. Mount Everest is the tallest mountain on Earth.

41
00:04:48,163 --> 00:04:51,813
Three. Volcanoes have hot, melted rock inside.

42
00:04:58,598 --> 00:05:04,387
Quiz time! Which is the tallest mountain on Earth? Mount Everest, or Nap Mountain?

43
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:09,679
Mount Everest! Well done!

44
00:05:12,273 --> 00:05:17,281
Next. What is inside a volcano? Hot chocolate, or hot melted rock?

45
00:05:20,474 --> 00:05:23,131
Hot melted rock! Sorry, Whiskers.

46
00:05:30,514 --> 00:05:33,229
And with a twinkle, they were home again.

47
00:05:33,429 --> 00:05:37,090
Ahh. Nap Mountain. My favourite mountain in the world.

48
00:05:37,290 --> 00:05:39,363
Goodnight, Tashi! Goodnight, Iggy!

49
00:05:43,155 --> 00:05:47,018
Next time, rivers and lakes! Goodnight, bumpy world.

